<title>ITALY: Italtel returns to profit in 1996, sales up.</title>
<headline>Italtel returns to profit in 1996, sales up.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian telecoms systems maker Italtel said it posted a 1996 consolidated net profit of five billion lire against a 1995 loss of 74 billion lire.</p>
<p>The company, jointly owned by Italian state telecoms holding Stet and Germany's Siemens AG, said in a statement that turnover rose 20 percent to 3.90 trillion lire, of which 1.52 trillion was from exports.</p>
<p>Chairman Salvatore Randi said the trend would continue in 1997. &quot;We have an encouraging order book both in the fixed and mobile network sectors,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
